      "content": "wait, did you just compare my pandas error to catching a goblin in a trap? lol\n\ni'm not really sure what you mean by that in a technical context. is \"goblin\" some kind of niche slang for memory fragmentation or something? i've been using pandas for years and i've never heard a dev refer to data pointers or indexing issues that way. \n\ncan we stick to the technical side? i really need to understand that part about the memory allocation and lazy evaluation you mentioned. why exactly does lazy evaluation make the warning pop up inconsistently?",
